From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:35:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: drop the mboxes reference in
 mailbox_chan_available

The fwnode conversion (sky1-ncz-v7.3-final-port.patch) replaced
of_parse_phandle_with_args(..., NULL) - which releases the node it looks
up internally - with fwnode_property_get_reference_args() storing the
result in a local fwnode_reference_args, and nothing ever released that
reference: every channel availability check leaked one reference to the
mboxes node.

ACPI fwnodes carry no refcount so only a DT boot is affected, but this is
an upstream driver and adding ACPI support must not regress the DT path.

Put the reference before returning. Same fix as cix-linux-main
0ed9fc938c60 ("scmi: release the mboxes reference taken by
mailbox_chan_available") and linux-cix 1b2eec81 fix #2 - independent
discovery on all three sides.

---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/transports/mailbox.c
@@ -93,8 +93,13 @@ static bool mailbox_chan_available(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode, int idx)
 	if (num_mb == 3 && idx == 1)
 		idx = 2;
 
-	return !fwnode_property_get_reference_args(fwnode, "mboxes",
-					   "#mbox-cells", 1, idx, &fwnode_args);
+	if (fwnode_property_get_reference_args(fwnode, "mboxes", "#mbox-cells",
+					       1, idx, &fwnode_args))
+		return false;
+
+	/* fwnode_property_get_reference_args() took a reference; drop it. */
+	fwnode_handle_put(fwnode_args.fwnode);
+	return true;
 }
 
